#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105508 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/id #uuid "7d104813-5c61-5696-912a-b29d6f012b28" :question/math-academy-id "e-4315" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 2, -3, -7 \\rangle$. Find $\\mid \\mathbf{a} \\mid$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2} + a_{z}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{2^{2} + (-3)^{2} + (-7)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4 + 9 + 49} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{62}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105509 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given the Coordinates of its Endpoints"}] :question/id #uuid "c0f385e3-6689-59d4-af2c-036e630f4303" :question/math-academy-id "e-4316" :question/problem "Let $A(1,1,2)$ and $B(2,-2,3)$. Find $\\mid \\overrightarrow{AB} \\mid$." :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a = i + j + 2k,; OB^(→) = b = 2i - 2j + 3k\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= OB^(→) - OA^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i - 2j + 3k) - (i + j + 2k) \\\\\n&= i - 3j + k\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid AB^(→) \\mid &= \\sqrt{1^{2} + (-3)^{2} + 1^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1 + 9 + 1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{11}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105510 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "76abe9ed-240e-589b-9317-78cae1ccf91b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4317" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = \\dfrac{\\mathbf{a}}{\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\, \\mid}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a \\mid &= \\sqrt{a_{x}^{2} + a_{y}^{2} + a_{z}^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + (-5)^{2} + 1^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{16 + 25 + 1} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{42}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a}{\\mid a \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{42}}a \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{42}} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}4/\\sqrt{42} \\\\ -5/\\sqrt{42} \\\\ 1/\\sqrt{42}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "674a1a46-57de-54a7-8487-70cbb3edb1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{86}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268013} {:answer/id #uuid "69c8502d-4cac-5125-94b4-e6b4dc00074c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{43}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268014} {:answer/id #uuid "e80dd57a-bacb-546d-a145-38f180876a67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{43}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268015} {:answer/id #uuid "3417ad40-5bd1-51db-ae6d-ddcf75e78652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268016} {:answer/id #uuid "56a18173-4be3-586b-b96f-75dfb5622ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{86}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268017}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "674a1a46-57de-54a7-8487-70cbb3edb1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{86}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268013} :answer-field/id #uuid "9191d942-077d-573d-a965-a53a7560110f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268012}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "67f4089b-8a03-5d8a-a5ab-7b4bb871ba4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-101003" :question/problem "Let $A(5,0,9)$ and $B(3,9,8).$ Find $|a-b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively." :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=5i+9k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=3i+9j+8k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a-b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a-b & =(5i+9k)-(3i+9j+8k) \\\\  & =2i-9j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a-b| & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-9)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+81+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{86}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268018 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "595818e4-7608-5319-8879-68af7ebd600c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268020} {:answer/id #uuid "0cf7fd18-68f7-5d5b-a739-d880bf2f1e02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268021} {:answer/id #uuid "c0f6c572-bb2e-50ae-b973-dc693af85c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268022} {:answer/id #uuid "61f2c3dd-7124-5c52-ab67-2350d99e05aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268023} {:answer/id #uuid "8f6987be-beef-53a1-9827-da8122beba19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268024}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61f2c3dd-7124-5c52-ab67-2350d99e05aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268023} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9b2af0e-0b1d-533b-bcda-fea92242b130" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268019}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "37c26371-ee5e-53be-9050-103fa05959ea" :question/math-academy-id "q-101015" :question/problem "Given that $c=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,c\\,| & =\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $c$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1}c \\\\  & =1\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268025 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given the Coordinates of its Endpoints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1eff147d-7991-5577-941f-dfefef771a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{2}},-\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268027} {:answer/id #uuid "e24ab795-753f-51df-a4e5-23471241d90f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268028} {:answer/id #uuid "f63024e9-c5d2-5550-aa05-d23ba72ca4db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268029} {:answer/id #uuid "3c8a0d37-81c7-5dff-b38d-e85609370fe6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}},-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268030} {:answer/id #uuid "fdebd7c2-31aa-553e-83c8-b92199c5d24e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268031}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f63024e9-c5d2-5550-aa05-d23ba72ca4db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268029} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c4f24e8-2b08-509d-8782-662496fe1685" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268026}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed7c86d6-fb53-53c2-abe3-3eb800a8608d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101022" :question/problem "Let $A(2,7,0)$ and $B(2,5,4).$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{AB}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2i+7j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=2i+5j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =2i+5j+4k-(2i+7j) \\\\  & =-2j+4k \\\\  & =⟨0,-2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,| & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+4+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{AB}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{5}}\\cdot ⟨0,-2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268032 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51c0a073-16f6-5075-ab79-082029fefc39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268034} {:answer/id #uuid "751c70b9-f198-5081-b5d2-f4b011a45533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268035} {:answer/id #uuid "01cf21bf-1d9b-52bc-9ed8-a0b81f0b1c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268036} {:answer/id #uuid "aea2f69d-9ad5-5eaf-9d63-ca8e6650f777" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268037} {:answer/id #uuid "4a5dc535-521e-515c-9334-539e36ae461e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "751c70b9-f198-5081-b5d2-f4b011a45533" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268035} :answer-field/id #uuid "e16c155b-f690-589b-9799-02350c692c18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268033}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1a5ff143-4b08-50ba-ab83-c7ad9794fdd8" :question/math-academy-id "q-120543" :question/problem "Given that $w=⟨-1,0,3⟩$, find $|\\,w\\,|.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,w\\,| & =\\sqrt{{w}_{x}^{2}+{w}_{y}^{2}+{w}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268039 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "73c2055e-2f92-5558-b2a3-7835d0fe4cab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268041} {:answer/id #uuid "c148fae9-42aa-54ad-899b-dbe2a8cd02d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268042} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd3c077-301d-5075-ae73-bf9245f1ad3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268043} {:answer/id #uuid "3fd5bc02-5ebf-5878-baba-aa6a3e38bf03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268044} {:answer/id #uuid "5162fb60-1334-532f-92f1-e04269cc7b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268045}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3dd3c077-301d-5075-ae73-bf9245f1ad3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268043} :answer-field/id #uuid "81db4113-6937-5623-8981-6dc3bbeb7700" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268040}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8236bfe8-e752-5be1-a0f1-42011f4d99a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-120546" :question/problem "Let $A(1,0,-1)$ and $B(0,1,1).$ Find $|a+2b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively." :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=i-k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=j+k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a+2b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(i-k)+2(j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+2b| & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268046 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given the Coordinates of its Endpoints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d4f8682-7e56-5c76-8be9-35af48c7e09b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268048} {:answer/id #uuid "f0ed6c28-59e3-505b-83ae-05e37746cf5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268049} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c9577e-1896-59d8-b930-6e9b9f755bd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268050} {:answer/id #uuid "327084be-a9cb-511b-bd8a-4a0bebcbb1ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268051} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd7219f-6907-5f1d-afba-8dbe888f807f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0ed6c28-59e3-505b-83ae-05e37746cf5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268049} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecba19e6-9a28-5e85-a00a-81683edd3f96" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268047}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d760a7fb-7cfa-5c14-a94a-ab89ef422900" :question/math-academy-id "q-18309" :question/problem "Let $A(5,-1,1)$ and $B(0,-2,3).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{AB}|.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=5i-j+k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=-2j+3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{OB}-\\overset{\\to }{OA} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j+3k)-(5i-j+k) \\\\  & =-5i-j+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+1+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106026 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe61b3a1-9e6d-55b4-b6b7-27c3bed2c392" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{74}}, \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{74}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{74}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102394} {:answer/id #uuid "186ff4db-a684-5234-a9fe-d4445b22cdd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{74}}, \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{74}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{74}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102395} {:answer/id #uuid "22ad60e1-fb01-562a-88b8-08b42c1e9884" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{77}},-\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}},-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102396} {:answer/id #uuid "28b4bc21-f68e-5747-965e-a89aa5afb118" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{77}}, \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102397} {:answer/id #uuid "49474f4b-2912-595f-95b0-9e42acee4bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{77}}, \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49474f4b-2912-595f-95b0-9e42acee4bb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨ - \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{77}}, \\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}}, \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102398} :answer-field/id #uuid "9edea1ff-b532-59c5-b499-57648c90c425" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102393}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "46dce84e-4f15-50e3-8511-5dd62cf1728a" :question/math-academy-id "q-18975" :question/problem "Let $a = ⟨ - 2, 8, 3⟩$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $a$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,a\\,| & =\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}+{a}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{8}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+64+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{77}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $a$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{a}{|\\,a\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{77}}a \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{77}}\\cdot ⟨-2,8,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{77}},\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{77}},\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{77}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268053 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0f0855f-67d1-5bbe-bc62-f378c8eddb59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268055} {:answer/id #uuid "6cdbe149-04ab-5ff6-9a42-6aab4426470a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268056} {:answer/id #uuid "e85c0d1d-f843-5670-9623-127449b9d4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268057} {:answer/id #uuid "499517ce-8370-587b-993c-91301caffa25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268058} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d8ecd1-ff3d-5b20-a571-e158d988a6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e85c0d1d-f843-5670-9623-127449b9d4c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268057} :answer-field/id #uuid "25e2a601-14e5-57e7-a166-5ec14a51289f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268054}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4aedad12-e4e4-5e62-ae83-35382ca40566" :question/math-academy-id "q-18977" :question/problem "Given that $c=⟨-1,0,1⟩$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $c.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{c}{|\\,c\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,c\\,| & =\\sqrt{{c}_{x}^{2}+{c}_{y}^{2}+{c}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+0+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $c$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{c}{|c|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}c \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot ⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268060 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36dccfda-4853-5561-980a-992914ea0c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268062}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "36dccfda-4853-5561-980a-992914ea0c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268062} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9ad6d6a-7f9e-5e2a-8741-100ce4cb292b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268061}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09cc540a-0811-50ab-be39-1fa66c3fe0c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-281595" :question/problem "Let $P(1,-2,4)$ and $Q(-3,0,5).$ Find $|q-p|,$ where $p$ and $q$ are position vectors of $P$ and $Q$, respectively.\n\n$|q-p|=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =p=i-2j+4k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OQ} & =q=-3i+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $q-p,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q-p & =(-3i+5k)-(i-2j+4k) \\\\  & =-4i+2j+k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|q-p| & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268063 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bef966c5-dfeb-5d2e-88f6-054d460a46b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268065} {:answer/id #uuid "348944cd-485a-5a2d-89d3-38c42c33c79d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268066}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bef966c5-dfeb-5d2e-88f6-054d460a46b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268065} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae50204b-f4a7-50a1-950e-93908aafa15c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268064} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b07c50d-63c8-54a0-8e9e-84b9f064ed61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7b07c50d-63c8-54a0-8e9e-84b9f064ed61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268068} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee458d5-4e9f-5487-a55d-1a9c17a9eda7" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268067}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9e5eb066-bcdc-5c6c-bd00-a9b20ee93a8d" :question/math-academy-id "q-281600" :question/problem "Given that $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$, find a unit vector that is parallel to $n.$\n\n|  |  | $-\\frac{2}{3}$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $u=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,n\\,| & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $n$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{n}{|\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}n \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268069 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given the Coordinates of its Endpoints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd417ad9-e6a2-589c-be4f-93c2f63606fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{89}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd417ad9-e6a2-589c-be4f-93c2f63606fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{89}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268071} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bfb3b44-e1e4-5492-8fd9-e32e311a31f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268070}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "da6cd2a0-d46a-5b1d-903b-d302fcd58f5e" :question/math-academy-id "q-281689" :question/problem "Let $C(2,4,-3)$ and $D(-1,0,5).$ Find $|\\overset{\\to }{DC}|.$\n\n$|\\overset{\\to }{DC}|=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OC} & =c=2i+4j-3k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OD} & =d=-i+5k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{DC}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DC} & =\\overset{\\to }{OC}-\\overset{\\to }{OD} \\\\  & =c-d \\\\  & =(2i+4j-3k)-(-i+5k) \\\\  & =3i+4j-8k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{DC}| & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{89}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given the Coordinates of its Endpoints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bca73923-98e8-597f-b98e-0c51dd30f950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bca73923-98e8-597f-b98e-0c51dd30f950" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268074} :answer-field/id #uuid "1d7b1a13-2fae-58e2-ba0f-db57c176bc23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20040203-50f8-5150-80b2-55422c07024c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268076}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20040203-50f8-5150-80b2-55422c07024c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268076} :answer-field/id #uuid "28e35acb-1c15-5bc8-a28d-8ac27319acad" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268075}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "29d6a356-c63e-5c97-b3cf-34173a5ab8fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-282324" :question/problem "Let $R(5,-3,2)$ and $S(1,-1,4).$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\overset{\\to }{SR}.$\n\n$u=⟨${{field-1}}$,\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =r=5i-3j+2k, \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{OS} & =s=i-j+4k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overset{\\to }{SR}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SR} & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}-\\overset{\\to }{OS} \\\\  & =r-s \\\\  & =(5i-3j+2k)-(i-j+4k) \\\\  & =4i-2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-2,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{SR}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{SR}\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{\\to }{SR}| & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+4+4} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\overset{\\to }{SR}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{\\overset{\\to }{SR}}{|\\,\\overset{\\to }{SR}\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{6}}\\overset{\\to }{SR} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot ⟨4,-2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}},\\,-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268077 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1916efa2-6a98-59a5-858c-c4fe64d8e8bc" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given the Coordinates of its Endpoints"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a2a4f49-1c19-57fb-9a47-02edfebab8e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268079} {:answer/id #uuid "c2579090-718e-57e8-8ad7-21842b355a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268080}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a2a4f49-1c19-57fb-9a47-02edfebab8e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268079} :answer-field/id #uuid "32e1507d-3844-5fe6-b8ec-acb94d8025a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7dd2998c-06ce-5201-bc18-2c28c9c17ac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268082}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7dd2998c-06ce-5201-bc18-2c28c9c17ac4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268082} :answer-field/id #uuid "ea830354-4a32-5044-aee0-4689e6cb87d6" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268081}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f574a23c-91ca-57cf-8977-20c4b56285cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-282351" :question/problem "Let $A(3,-2,-1)$ and $B(3,-2,0).$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $-2a+b.$\n\n$u=⟨${{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$,\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}⟩$" :question/worked-solution "First, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=3i-2j-k, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=3i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $-2a+b$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2a+b & =-2(3i-2j-k)+(3i-2j) \\\\  & =-6i+4j+2k+3i-2j \\\\  & =-3i+2j+2k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{-2a+b}{|\\,-2a+b\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|u| & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+4+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we divide the vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{17}}\\cdot ⟨-3,2,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{17}},\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}},\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{17}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268083 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d766de83-9394-57be-84a4-bb88f5ddf792" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Magnitude of a Vector Given in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85a9d8f8-65da-5299-8573-c07fac97a7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{103}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268085} {:answer/id #uuid "ad0918e2-668d-5b3d-a358-cbc9bad7897e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268086} {:answer/id #uuid "b992565f-df29-5c4a-a4b0-dd51fa1b2908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{101}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268087} {:answer/id #uuid "89553c56-3ebe-53f6-8083-a53c4e80d44a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{102}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268088} {:answer/id #uuid "1af54d5b-75af-57f3-9136-aefd064108b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b992565f-df29-5c4a-a4b0-dd51fa1b2908" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{101}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268087} :answer-field/id #uuid "960015a6-e2d4-5760-b835-46450522c98c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268084}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "987674d8-6a5b-5010-97df-7f67935f50cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-70425" :question/problem "Let $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(1,3,-3).$ Find $|a+2b|,$ where $a$ and $b$ are position vectors of $A$ and $B$, respectively." :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=i+3j-3k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the coordinates of $a+2b$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+2b & =(2i+j)+2(i+3j-3k) \\\\  & =4i+7j-6k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+2b| & =\\sqrt{(4)^{2}+(7)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+49+36} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{101}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268090 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "83423c03-d314-5f78-9acf-58cbb6f7774b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a71b06b0-fb26-5ce9-af8c-f3efed43861f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{26}},0,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{26}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268092} {:answer/id #uuid "aa3a865d-72dd-55fd-9ade-4c029df7b76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{23}},0,\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{23}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268093} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a2405a-2453-500b-93b8-2857c42c4c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{5},0,\\frac{3}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268094} {:answer/id #uuid "bdacf46e-c1a3-5672-a5a1-23da5e669d11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{3}},0,\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268095} {:answer/id #uuid "892330d6-9f66-5b8f-bb9f-6e9413045c75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}},0,\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{6}}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268096}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a0a2405a-2453-500b-93b8-2857c42c4c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-\\frac{4}{5},0,\\frac{3}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268094} :answer-field/id #uuid "b71d6cb0-c834-5f2f-8302-599f0e0053ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268091}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9d11fcaf-d601-5df3-a05e-e3ba6cc96f97" :question/math-academy-id "q-70430" :question/problem "Let $v=⟨-4,0,3⟩.$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $v.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{v}{|\\,v\\,|}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\,v\\,| & =\\sqrt{{v}_{x}^{2}+{v}_{y}^{2}+{v}_{z}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+0+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $v$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & =\\frac{v}{|\\,v\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}v \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ⟨-4,0,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{4}{5},0,\\frac{3}{5}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
